stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> DETECTED: R1 watcher hit, drift report or rejection pattern
    DETECTED --> TRIAGED: R2 source captured raw and rendered, classified
    TRIAGED --> NO_CHANGE: R3 no impact, a second analyst concurs
    TRIAGED --> DRAFTING: R4 change needed
    DRAFTING --> IN_REVIEW: R5 citation, corrigendum check, impact and golden cases attached
    IN_REVIEW --> DRAFTING: R6 returned with reasons
    IN_REVIEW --> REJECTED: R7 rejected with reasons
    IN_REVIEW --> CERTIFYING: R8 independent qualified reviewer approves
    CERTIFYING --> DRAFTING: R9 a golden case or portal fixture diverges
    CERTIFYING --> STAGED: R10 every case reproduces, signed pack built
    STAGED --> PUBLISHED: R11 canary clean, live before first use
    PUBLISHED --> SUPERSEDED: R12 newer version for the same scope
    PUBLISHED --> ROLLED_BACK: R13 defect found, two approvers
    TRIAGED --> WITHDRAWN: R14 instrument withdrawn or stayed
    DRAFTING --> WITHDRAWN: R14 instrument withdrawn or stayed
    IN_REVIEW --> WITHDRAWN: R14 instrument withdrawn or stayed
    CERTIFYING --> WITHDRAWN: R14 instrument withdrawn or stayed
    STAGED --> WITHDRAWN: R14 instrument withdrawn or stayed
    STAGED --> DRAFTING: R15 canary shows a defect
    NO_CHANGE --> [*]
    REJECTED --> [*]
    WITHDRAWN --> [*]
    SUPERSEDED --> [*]
    ROLLED_BACK --> [*]

    note right of TRIAGED
      Amendments and corrigenda are change
      requests, not news items - every
      published rule watches its base instrument.
    end note

    note right of PUBLISHED
      Old versions stay queryable forever.
      A rollback publishes a superseding
      version, never a deletion.
    end note
